# FACTORY (the author, 2026-10-05): `@: h f(a)` receives a factory's result; this row wrote `h: f a` until then.
# steps/merge-callable-r48.md S1 (REVIEW ebae3b0, fable_pc's M57): a held callable with a size_t header called from a
# method -- its argument goes in a size_t cell and its result comes back in the size_t variant's cell, so add5(1U) is
# 6U.  An int cell in the argument's place would hand the helper a cell of another type.  Entry 7.
fn: makeAdder (size_t: n) fn: (size_t: x) size_t
    fn: addN (size_t: x) size_t
        return: n + x
    return: addN
@: add5 makeAdder(5U)
fn: go () int
    size_t: a (add5: 1U)
    if: a = 6U
        return: 7
    return: 81
int: r 0
r: go()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
